The worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28th, the system showed it had been shipped, but I did not receive the goods until October 12th.
Checking the status of an Amazon order, the seller did not provide a tracking number, so I can't find where the order is.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide a tracking number, but received no response after two days.
As a last resort, I contacted Amazon customer service, who revealed the seller's phone number. I called the store, and after a few attempts, the call connected. The seller informed me that the package had been lost and that I could have a new one sent to me immediately.
Although I was very angry, since the computer was urgently needed, I didn't say much to the seller and just asked for it to be sent to me immediately.
So, the next day, I called to ask if it had shipped yet?
The seller says it's not available yet; it will be shipped in the afternoon.
I called again in the afternoon, and the seller said they would definitely ship it, with shipment after 5 or 6 PM in the afternoon. However, when I called at 7 PM, there was no answer.
On the third morning, I called again to ask if the shipment had been sent out?
Can you tell me the order number?
The seller said they haven't shipped it yet. They told me to order from another vendor if I'm in a hurry, and that if I can wait, they will ship it later in the afternoon.
There’s no way around it; I have to wait for hours to order something from another store.
All I can do is beg the seller to ship quickly.
Finally, after countless phone calls, I received the computer on October 16.
